examples.question_text:
The graph of $y=f(x)$ consists of the two line segments shown. Sketch $y=\frac12f(x)$, marking the images of the three labelled points.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-4)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (-3,-3)--(0,2)--(3,2);
\fill[black] (-3,-3) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(-3,-3)$};
\fill[black] (0,2) circle (1.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,2)$};
\fill[black] (3,2) circle (1.5pt) node[above right] {$(3,2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Multiply each $y$-coordinate by $\frac12$ and keep each $x$-coordinate.

$\begin{aligned}(-3,-3)&\mapsto(-3,-\tfrac32)\\(0,2)&\mapsto(0,1)\\(3,2)&\mapsto(3,1)\end{aligned}$

Join the image points with line segments. The dashed graph is $y=f(x)$; the blue graph is $y=\frac12f(x)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mappedBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-4)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-3,-3)--(0,2)--(3,2);
\draw[mappedBlue,thick] (-3,-1.5)--(0,1)--(3,1);
\fill[mappedBlue] (-3,-1.5) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(-3,-\frac32)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (0,1) circle (1.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,1)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (3,1) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(3,1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

