examples.solution_text:
The horizontal dilation factor is $\frac13$. Divide each $x$-coordinate by $3$ and keep each $y$-coordinate.

$\begin{aligned}(-3,-3)&\mapsto(-1,-3)\\(0,2)&\mapsto(0,2)\\(3,2)&\mapsto(1,2)\end{aligned}$

Join the image points with line segments. The dashed graph is $y=f(x)$; the blue graph is $y=f(3x)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mappedBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-4)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-3,-3)--(0,2)--(3,2);
\draw[mappedBlue,thick] (-1,-3)--(0,2)--(1,2);
\fill[mappedBlue] (-1,-3) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(-1,-3)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (0,2) circle (1.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,2)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (1,2) circle (1.5pt) node[above right] {$(1,2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

