examples.solution_text:
Combine a horizontal dilation of factor $\frac13$ with a vertical dilation of factor $\frac12$.

$(x,y)\mapsto\left(\frac{x}{3},\frac{y}{2}\right)$

$\begin{aligned}(-3,-3)&\mapsto(-1,-\tfrac32)\\(0,2)&\mapsto(0,1)\\(3,2)&\mapsto(1,1)\end{aligned}$

Join the image points with line segments. The dashed graph is $y=f(x)$; the blue graph is $y=\frac12f(3x)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mappedBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-4)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-3,-3)--(0,2)--(3,2);
\draw[mappedBlue,thick] (-1,-1.5)--(0,1)--(1,1);
\fill[mappedBlue] (-1,-1.5) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(-1,-\frac32)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (0,1) circle (1.5pt) node[above left] {$(0,1)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (1,1) circle (1.5pt) node[below right] {$(1,1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
The dashed curve is $f(x)=\sqrt{x}$. The blue curve is a vertical dilation of it. Use the labelled points to find the dilation factor and write $g(x)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mappedBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-0.7,0)--(10.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.7)--(0,7.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed,thick,->,domain=0:10,samples=81,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{sqrt(\x)});
\draw[mappedBlue,thick,->,domain=0:10,samples=81,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*sqrt(\x)});
\node at (5.5,1.6) {$f(x)=\sqrt{x}$};
\node[mappedBlue] at (4,5.5) {$g(x)$};
\fill[black] (9,3) circle (1.5pt) node[below left] {$(9,3)$};
\fill[mappedBlue] (9,6) circle (1.5pt) node[above left] {$(9,6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
